Cherry-pick of upstream PR https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/32963
("fix(agent): recover Codex Responses streams with null output") ported onto
v2026.5.16. Upstream authored the fix against post-tag `main` where the codex
runtime had been extracted into agent/codex_runtime.py; in v2026.5.16 that
logic still lives in run_agent.py (_run_codex_stream /
_run_codex_create_stream_fallback), so the codex-side hunks are re-targeted
there. The auxiliary_client.py hunks and test hunks are upstream verbatim
(applied with line-offset). The scripts/release.py AUTHOR_MAP hunk is dropped
— it adds a contributor mapping for the upstream release script and is not
relevant to the runtime fix.

